INTERVIEW QUESTION 1
What is GitHub Copilot?
=======================

Interview Answer:

GitHub Copilot is an AI-powered coding assistant built using
Generative AI models. It helps developers by providing real-time code
suggestions, completing code, generating functions from comments,
creating documentation, and assisting with test case generation.

It improves developer productivity by reducing repetitive coding tasks
and speeding up software development.

---

Key Points

✔ AI-powered coding assistant

✔ Built using Generative AI models

✔ Works inside the IDE

✔ Provides real-time code suggestions

✔ Improves developer productivity

======================================================================
INTERVIEW QUESTION 2
How does GitHub Copilot work?
=============================

Interview Answer:

GitHub Copilot works as an AI pair programmer. As the developer types
code or writes comments, Copilot reads the surrounding code context and
sends it to its AI model.

The AI analyzes the context, predicts the most relevant code, and
returns real-time suggestions inside the IDE. The developer can accept,
modify, or reject these suggestions.

---

Working Flow

Developer writes code/comment
│
▼
Copilot reads surrounding context
│
▼
AI model analyzes the request
│
▼
Generates code suggestions
│
▼
Developer Accepts / Edits / Rejects

